  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "An owner evaluating **branded residences** for a hotel project in Mexico should primarily consider the luxury hotel groups already active or expanding there: **Marriott** brands such as **Ritz-Carlton, St. Regis, W, and Four Points by Sheraton**; **Four Seasons**; **Auberge Resorts Collection**; **Rosewood**; **Montage**; **Hyatt** brands such as **Thompson, Park Hyatt, and Kimpton**; **Hilton** brands such as **Conrad, Waldorf Astoria, and Hilton**; and **Accor** brands such as **Fairmont, Banyan Tree, SLS, Mondrian, MGallery, and Hyde**.[1][2][3][4][5][6][7][8][11][14][16][17]\n\nFor a Mexico-specific shortlist, the brands most repeatedly cited across current projects are **Ritz-Carlton**, **St. Regis**, **Four Seasons**, **Rosewood**, **Auberge**, **Montage**, **Thompson**, **Viceroy**, **Aman**, **Fairmont**, **Banyan Tree**, **MGallery**, **SLS**, **Hyde**, **Conrad**, **Waldorf Astoria**, **Kimpton**, and **Park Hyatt**.[1][2][3][4][5][8][9][10][11][14][15][18][20]\n\nA practical way to narrow the field is by positioning:\n- **Ultra-luxury / trophy asset**: **Aman, Four Seasons, Rosewood, Ritz-Carlton, St. Regis**.[1][3][4][9][18][20]\n- **Design-forward luxury**: **Montage, Auberge, Viceroy, Thompson, SLS, Banyan Tree**.[1][2][3][4][9][15][18][20]\n- **Urban / branded lifestyle**: **W, Park Hyatt, Kimpton, The Standard, Thompson, Giorgio Armani residences**.[1][4][6][10][16][17]\n- **Value-leaning luxury or wider distribution**: **Hilton/Conrad, Fairmont, MGallery, Hyde**.[3][8][11][14][17]\n\nIf you want, I can turn this into a **brand-by-brand comparison for Mexico** based on **project type, target buyer, and likely fee structure**.",
